Static JAL calls take a lean inline path (PS2Runtime::callGuestFunction) instead of the full dispatchGuestBranch.
Same checkpoint charge, function-table entry (overrides still apply), missing-function handling and return checks;
no branch trace ring, dispatch history, perf hook or trace getenv tests per call. Full dispatch: GOW_DISPATCH_FULL=1,
PS2X_GS_WORKER_TRACE, calls to GOW_PERF_FRAME_PC, missing targets; PS2X_STATIC_CALLS=dispatch at recompile time emits
the old call. Micro-benchmark (empty callee, Linux clang -O2): 9.5 -> 6.3 ns per call. Tests: parity with DirectCall.

